Hi Ilhami,

Simon Urbanek wrote [2011-05-25 15:17]:
>
> On May 25, 2011, at 4:43 AM, Ilhami Visne wrote:
>
>> Hello,
>>
>> I could not install rJava on a Centos 5.5 machine, although i
>> called first R CMD javareconf. Below some informations to track
>> down the problem.
>>
>
> Your JDK is incomplete, look at the empty entry in the javareconf
> result, you're missing javah (Java headers generator).

The JDK is probably complete, but its installer didn't create a link for 
javah in the /usr/bin directory. R expect javah in /usr/bin, it doesn't 
check the java home directory. You can create the link manually as root:

ln -s /usr/java/default/bin/javah /usr/bin

Simon, is it possible to force R that it picks only JAVA_HOME and not 
the links in /usr/bin?

Regards,
Stephan


